WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.052 --> 00:00:03.353
president, Elizabeth Warren

00:00:03.387 --> 00:00:04.454
because they could not raise the

00:00:04.588 --> 00:00:04.822
money --

00:00:04.955 --> 00:00:06.290
&gt;&gt; I want be to press pause for

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.891
a second because the house

00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:09.393
speaker, Kevin Mccarthy, just

00:00:09.526 --> 00:00:10.594
walked out of his meeting from

00:00:10.727 --> 00:00:11.595
the white house.

00:00:11.728 --> 00:00:13.497
Let's listen.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.365
&gt;&gt; I don't want to put any words

00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:16.466
in his mouth.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.701
We had an hour conversation

00:00:17.835 --> 00:00:20.771
about this, that I thought was a

00:00:20.904 --> 00:00:22.005
very good discussion and we

00:00:22.139 --> 00:00:24.107
walked out saying we would

00:00:24.241 --> 00:00:24.942
continue the discussion.

00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:28.612
And I think there is an

00:00:28.745 --> 00:00:31.615
opportunity here to come to an

00:00:31.748 --> 00:00:32.549
agreement on both sides.

00:00:32.749 --> 00:00:33.917
I think that's what the American

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:34.985
people want.

00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:36.420
They want us to be responsible

00:00:36.553 --> 00:00:37.521
and sensible about this.

00:00:37.654 --> 00:00:39.389
That's exactly the way we're

00:00:39.389 --> 00:00:39.690
handling it.

00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:40.824
I told the president I would

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.559
like to see if we could come to

00:00:42.693 --> 00:00:43.861
an agreement long before the

00:00:43.994 --> 00:00:45.395
deadline and we can start

00:00:45.529 --> 00:00:46.597
working on other things.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.098
&gt;&gt; Where should those budget

00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:52.903
cuts come from right now?

00:00:53.036 --> 00:00:53.670
Medicare and social security.

00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:54.204
What cuts --

00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:56.006
&gt;&gt; Well, let me be clear about

00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:56.373
that.

00:00:56.506 --> 00:00:58.609
No, we're not talking about

00:00:58.742 --> 00:00:58.909
that.

00:00:59.042 --> 00:01:00.544
To really be able to do this

00:01:00.677 --> 00:01:04.147
right, I'm not going to

00:01:04.281 --> 00:01:05.916
negotiate this in the press,

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:06.216
right?

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:07.417
I respect the conversation we

00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:10.020
had together and we will

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:10.487
continue that.

00:01:10.621 --> 00:01:12.022
&gt;&gt; You have a big plan.

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:13.423
When are you going to share that

00:01:13.423 --> 00:01:13.724
big plan?

00:01:13.857 --> 00:01:15.425
&gt;&gt; Look, I think the president

00:01:15.425 --> 00:01:16.627
and I have talked about a lot of

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.995
different ideas and we'll work

00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:21.431
to see if we can come to an

00:01:21.565 --> 00:01:21.899
agreement.

00:01:22.032 --> 00:01:23.433
Look, I know you -- I know you

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.535
all have a job to do, but I

00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:27.537
don't think we'll come to an

00:01:27.671 --> 00:01:28.672
agreement if I negotiate with

00:01:28.805 --> 00:01:28.939
you.

00:01:29.072 --> 00:01:30.874
I think the respectful way to do

00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:32.175
it is to talk to the president

00:01:32.309 --> 00:01:33.744
as we did right now for more

00:01:33.877 --> 00:01:34.711
than an hour.

00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:36.146
We both walked away.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.248
We have different perspectives

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:41.518
but we both laid out some of our

00:01:41.652 --> 00:01:43.687
vision of where we'd want to get

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.455
to and I believe after laying

00:01:45.455 --> 00:01:47.457
them both out, I can see where

00:01:47.457 --> 00:01:48.392
we can find common ground.

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:49.760
I think the American public

00:01:49.893 --> 00:01:50.994
would appreciate that.

00:01:51.128 --> 00:01:52.529
Look, I've been very -- I've

00:01:52.663 --> 00:01:53.497
been very clear.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.465
The current path we're on we

00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:56.466
cannot sustain.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.736
We've got to change the

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:00.938
trajectory to put ourselves on a

00:02:01.071 --> 00:02:01.805
path to balance.

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:03.540
How we get there will be our

00:02:03.674 --> 00:02:03.974
discussions.

00:02:04.107 --> 00:02:05.742
&gt;&gt; Mr. Speaker, do you have a

00:02:05.876 --> 00:02:07.644
chance to talk with president

00:02:07.778 --> 00:02:10.881
Biden about supporting Ukraine?

00:02:11.014 --> 00:02:15.085
And can those budget cuts impact

00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:16.119
support for Ukraine?

00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:18.522
&gt;&gt; Look, what we talked about

00:02:18.655 --> 00:02:20.023
today was about moving forward

00:02:20.157 --> 00:02:23.026
and how we move through the debt

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.995
ceiling and how we get an

00:02:25.128 --> 00:02:25.495
agreement.

00:02:25.495 --> 00:02:26.797
I believe if we're able to get

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.498
to an agreement, we could have a

00:02:28.632 --> 00:02:29.633
funding agreement for the next

00:02:29.766 --> 00:02:30.400
two years.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.569
You won't see omnibuses anymore.

00:02:32.703 --> 00:02:34.271
You'll see the senate and the

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:35.906
house actually do the job the

00:02:36.039 --> 00:02:37.507
American public has elected them

00:02:37.507 --> 00:02:39.977
to do, to walk through the

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.011
appropriation process which is

00:02:41.144 --> 00:02:42.612
the manner in which you do it

00:02:42.746 --> 00:02:43.847
where the American public can

00:02:43.981 --> 00:02:45.148
see where we're spending our

00:02:45.515 --> 00:02:46.516
money and I think there's a lot

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.185
of savings we can find for the

00:02:48.318 --> 00:02:49.519
American taxpayer.

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:51.188
This is the hard working

00:02:51.521 --> 00:02:51.555
taxpayers.

00:02:51.688 --> 00:02:53.657
I know there's a lot of places

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.125
where there's wasteful

00:02:55.525 --> 00:02:56.059
Washington spending.

00:02:56.226 --> 00:03:00.630
I find that we can find an

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:01.698
agreement.

00:03:01.832 --> 00:03:04.568
&gt;&gt; Warning you against visiting

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:05.135
Taiwan.

00:03:05.535 --> 00:03:07.204
Any reaction to China's warning

00:03:07.537 --> 00:03:08.472
against visiting Taiwan?

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:09.840
&gt;&gt; I don't think China can tell

00:03:09.973 --> 00:03:13.543
me where I can go at any time,

00:03:13.543 --> 00:03:14.945
any place.

00:03:15.078 --> 00:03:15.545
Listen --

00:03:15.545 --> 00:03:16.613
&gt;&gt; When will you share your

00:03:16.747 --> 00:03:18.048
plans, Mr. Speaker?

00:03:18.181 --> 00:03:19.049
&gt;&gt; The president and I are

00:03:19.182 --> 00:03:20.684
trying to find a way that we can

00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:21.118
work together.

00:03:21.551 --> 00:03:27.557
We will continue to do that.

00:03:27.557 --> 00:03:28.291
Yes, sir.

00:03:28.425 --> 00:03:30.327
&gt;&gt; When they see this national

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:33.063
debt, $31 trillion growing and

00:03:33.196 --> 00:03:34.998
growing, worried their kids'

00:03:35.132 --> 00:03:36.500
future is going to be buried in

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:38.001
that mounting debt.

00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:39.569
What do you tell those parents?

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:40.337
&gt;&gt; I tell those parents there,

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.571
that's why I'm here.

00:03:41.571 --> 00:03:42.973
That's why I'm here, to make

00:03:43.106 --> 00:03:44.307
sure their children do not have

00:03:44.441 --> 00:03:45.575
to continue this debt.

00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:47.577
If you just look, if we continue

00:03:47.577 --> 00:03:49.579
the trajectory we're on, in the

00:03:49.579 --> 00:03:51.748
next ten years we'll spend $8

00:03:51.882 --> 00:03:53.784
trillion just on interest.

00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:56.019
$8 trillion just on interest.

00:03:56.153 --> 00:03:57.587
What that means though, too,

00:03:57.587 --> 00:03:58.655
because of the spending that has

00:03:58.789 --> 00:04:00.824
been going on is that's why you

00:04:00.957 --> 00:04:02.759
have inflation.

00:04:02.893 --> 00:04:04.428
America's strength will shrink.

00:04:04.561 --> 00:04:05.862
Everyone has always said it

00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:07.931
doesn't matter what occupation,

00:04:08.065 --> 00:04:09.800
whether you're a U.S. General or

00:04:09.933 --> 00:04:11.601
not, the greatest threat to

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:12.502
America is our debt.

00:04:12.636 --> 00:04:17.040
Our debt is now at 120% of gdp,

00:04:17.174 --> 00:04:18.742
meaning our debt is larger than

00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:19.609
our economy.

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:21.611
This is higher than at any time

00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:23.613
in American history.

00:04:23.613 --> 00:04:25.715
And it's higher at any time in

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:26.983
American history when the

00:04:27.117 --> 00:04:28.218
revenues that are coming into

00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:29.619
government are higher than any

00:04:29.619 --> 00:04:32.622
other

00:04:32.756 --> 00:04:34.691
so we've got a lot of revenue,

00:04:34.825 --> 00:04:36.393
we just got a spending problem.

00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:37.928
So that's why I want to find

00:04:38.061 --> 00:04:38.528
common ground.

00:04:38.662 --> 00:04:41.765
&gt;&gt; Can you commit that the U.S.

00:04:41.898 --> 00:04:43.633
Will not default?

00:04:43.633 --> 00:04:45.202
&gt;&gt; Look, if I look at anything,

00:04:45.635 --> 00:04:47.637
and you want to equate this, if

00:04:47.637 --> 00:04:49.639
you have a child and you give

00:04:49.639 --> 00:04:50.841
them a credit card and they

00:04:50.974 --> 00:04:52.976
spend that limit, you're

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:54.177
responsible for paying that

00:04:54.311 --> 00:04:54.644
credit card.

00:04:54.778 --> 00:04:57.647
But the responsible thing going

00:04:57.647 --> 00:04:58.815
forward, not just raise the

00:04:58.949 --> 00:04:59.783
limit, but look at how you're

00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:03.954
spending.

00:05:04.087 --> 00:05:05.789
I look at chuck Schumer.

00:05:05.922 --> 00:05:08.425
He's never passed a real budget

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:09.960
or any appropriation bills, but

00:05:10.093 --> 00:05:13.830
puts a $1.7 trillion omnibus

00:05:13.964 --> 00:05:15.665
coming through?

00:05:15.665 --> 00:05:17.167
The American public doesn't want

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:17.901
that.

00:05:18.034 --> 00:05:19.202
They don't want government to

00:05:19.336 --> 00:05:20.737
take more of their hard-earned

00:05:20.871 --> 00:05:22.005
money or to waste it.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:23.673
So now is a moment in time, we

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.775
have five more months, I just

00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:26.977
walked out having an hour

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.145
conversation with this

00:05:28.278 --> 00:05:29.980
president, that I tell you in

00:05:30.113 --> 00:05:31.114
perspective was a good

00:05:31.248 --> 00:05:31.681
conversation.

00:05:31.681 --> 00:05:34.317
No agreements, no promises,

00:05:34.451 --> 00:05:35.685
except we will continue this

00:05:35.685 --> 00:05:35.952
conversation.

00:05:36.086 --> 00:05:38.188
I want to continue it on behalf

00:05:38.321 --> 00:05:39.689
of the American people and the

00:05:39.823 --> 00:05:41.892
parents, on behalf of every

00:05:42.025 --> 00:05:43.693
taxpayer here that we put

00:05:43.693 --> 00:05:45.695
ourselves on a trajectory that

00:05:45.695 --> 00:05:49.699
makes America stronger, secure,

00:05:49.699 --> 00:05:54.004
and balanced.

00:05:54.137 --> 00:05:55.705
Who has not asked a question?

00:05:55.705 --> 00:05:58.308
&gt;&gt; Mr. Speaker, what credibility

00:05:58.441 --> 00:05:59.709
do conservatives and Republicans

00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:02.279
have to talk about reducing

00:06:02.412 --> 00:06:02.679
deficit --

00:06:02.812 --> 00:06:06.049
&gt;&gt; That's a great question.

00:06:06.183 --> 00:06:07.083
&gt;&gt; -- When Republicans had

00:06:07.217 --> 00:06:08.285
control of the white house and

00:06:08.418 --> 00:06:09.719
congress, ran up the bill?

00:06:09.719 --> 00:06:11.788
&gt;&gt; Let's just go by the sheer

00:06:11.922 --> 00:06:13.723
facts and figures, all right?

00:06:13.723 --> 00:06:15.292
So Republicans were in the

00:06:15.725 --> 00:06:16.293
majority for eight years, and

00:06:16.426 --> 00:06:18.595
the Democrats came in the

00:06:18.728 --> 00:06:19.829
majority for the last four

00:06:19.963 --> 00:06:20.130
years.

00:06:20.263 --> 00:06:22.432
So in the last four years, the

00:06:22.566 --> 00:06:24.568
Democrats have increased

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.269
discretionary spending by 30%,

00:06:26.403 --> 00:06:27.737
over $400 billion.

00:06:27.737 --> 00:06:29.339
When the Republicans were a

00:06:29.739 --> 00:06:31.741
majority twice that long, the

00:06:31.841 --> 00:06:32.442
discretionary spending went down

00:06:32.576 --> 00:06:35.145
$10 billion.

00:06:35.278 --> 00:06:39.416
So I think the credibility lasts

00:06:39.749 --> 00:06:40.584
easily with the Republicans.

00:06:40.717 --> 00:06:44.387
If you want to argue from a

00:06:44.521 --> 00:06:49.192
place where the past president,

00:06:49.326 --> 00:06:51.761
if you continue down the same

00:06:51.761 --> 00:06:53.830
path, this presidency will put

00:06:53.964 --> 00:06:57.300
us in much greater debt.

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:58.935
So I'm in a place of being

00:06:59.069 --> 00:06:59.869
speaker of the house.

00:07:00.003 --> 00:07:01.771
My role right now is to make

00:07:01.771 --> 00:07:05.108
sure we have a sensible,

00:07:05.241 --> 00:07:06.810
responsible ability to raise the

00:07:06.943 --> 00:07:08.778
debt ceiling, but not continue

00:07:08.912 --> 00:07:10.246
this runaway spending.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.783
This is a moment in time that,

00:07:13.817 --> 00:07:16.152
for all American households,

00:07:16.286 --> 00:07:18.622
every family does this, every

00:07:18.755 --> 00:07:20.056
business does this, every state

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.791
government, every county

00:07:21.791 --> 00:07:22.258
government.

00:07:22.392 --> 00:07:26.763
When they have spent too much,

00:07:26.896 --> 00:07:28.965
they can look where waste is at,

00:07:29.099 --> 00:07:30.767
look where investments would be

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.535
better, and sit down and talk in

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:33.803
an adult fashion.

00:07:33.903 --> 00:07:34.838
That's the conversation I just

00:07:34.971 --> 00:07:36.406
had with the president, and

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:38.408
that's the conversation I want

00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:39.142
to continue so we can come to an

00:07:39.275 --> 00:07:44.681
agreement.

00:07:44.814 --> 00:07:46.950
[ Inaudible question ]

00:07:47.083 --> 00:07:48.551
&gt;&gt; Look, I don't need a

00:07:48.685 --> 00:07:49.819
commission to tell me where

00:07:49.819 --> 00:07:51.321
there's waste, fraud, and abuse.

00:07:51.821 --> 00:07:52.856
I don't need a commission to

00:07:52.989 --> 00:07:54.791
tell wrus we are spending too

00:07:54.924 --> 00:07:55.258
much.

00:07:55.392 --> 00:07:57.827
I don't need a commission to

00:07:57.927 --> 00:08:00.830
tell us we're in $31 trillion

00:08:00.964 --> 00:08:01.297
debt.

00:08:01.431 --> 00:08:02.499
Nobody needs to tell us that we

00:08:02.632 --> 00:08:04.934
have spent too much.

00:08:05.068 --> 00:08:07.103
Just like any family.

00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.438
So we don't need a commission to

00:08:08.571 --> 00:08:11.341
tell us to do our job that the

00:08:11.474 --> 00:08:16.212
American public elected us to

00:08:16.346 --> 00:08:16.479
do.

00:08:16.613 --> 00:08:19.482
For the next five months, we can

00:08:19.849 --> 00:08:22.485
sit down and solve this problem.

00:08:22.619 --> 00:08:30.560
[ Inaudible question ]

00:08:30.694 --> 00:08:32.696
&gt;&gt; I did not talk to him about

00:08:32.829 --> 00:08:34.297
classified documents.

00:08:34.431 --> 00:08:35.865
I came down here to talk about

00:08:35.865 --> 00:08:37.200
the debt ceiling and our

00:08:37.333 --> 00:08:37.867
spending.

00:08:37.867 --> 00:08:38.268
That's what we spent our time

00:08:38.401 --> 00:08:53.416
on

00:08:53.883 --> 00:08:54.050
.

00:08:54.184 --> 00:08:57.420
&gt;&gt; Right now, this is a

00:08:57.554 --> 00:08:58.988
conversation about mine with the

00:08:59.122 --> 00:09:00.290
president when it comes to the

00:09:00.423 --> 00:09:02.892
debt ceiling and spending.

00:09:03.026 --> 00:09:06.096
[ Inaudible question ]

00:09:06.229 --> 00:09:09.899
&gt;&gt; Look, we talked in different

00:09:09.899 --> 00:09:11.401
perspectives, as our first

00:09:11.534 --> 00:09:13.369
conversation about this.

00:09:13.503 --> 00:09:14.504
Look, I don't want to give any

00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:15.905
false impressions.

00:09:15.905 --> 00:09:18.675
He gave me his perspective, I

00:09:18.808 --> 00:09:20.410
gave him our perspective.

00:09:20.543 --> 00:09:24.814
But I believe in hearing both

00:09:24.948 --> 00:09:26.316
perspectives, be it family,

00:09:26.449 --> 00:09:28.184
relationships, that you can find

00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:29.919
common ground.

00:09:29.919 --> 00:09:33.923
There's nothing in there that

00:09:34.023 --> 00:09:35.925
does not believe that we can

00:09:35.925 --> 00:09:37.560
come to an agreement that makes

00:09:37.927 --> 00:09:39.929
America stronger, puts us on a

00:09:39.929 --> 00:09:41.197
path to balance and exactly what

00:09:41.331 --> 00:09:42.499
the American people are asking

00:09:42.632 --> 00:09:43.566
us to do.

00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:44.267
It's our responsibility to do

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.302
it.

00:09:46.436 --> 00:09:47.937
&gt;&gt; Even if you do reach an

00:09:47.937 --> 00:09:48.938
agreement with the president,

00:09:49.072 --> 00:09:49.939
are you concerned that members

00:09:49.939 --> 00:09:51.941
of your own party won't go along

00:09:52.041 --> 00:09:52.408
with it?

00:09:52.542 --> 00:09:53.209
&gt;&gt; No.

00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:55.078
We just met today in a

00:09:55.211 --> 00:09:55.478
conference.

00:09:55.612 --> 00:09:58.448
Look, the Republicans are very

00:09:58.581 --> 00:09:58.782
united.

00:09:58.915 --> 00:10:01.251
Had we not been elected to the

00:10:01.384 --> 00:10:02.652
majority, we wouldn't be having

00:10:02.786 --> 00:10:03.486
this discussion.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.487
The American people would not

00:10:04.621 --> 00:10:06.890
have an advocate here to curve

00:10:07.023 --> 00:10:07.557
the waste and the spending

00:10:07.957 --> 00:10:09.159
that's happening.

00:10:09.292 --> 00:10:11.027
So I think this is a positive.

00:10:11.161 --> 00:10:13.429
This is exactly how government

00:10:13.563 --> 00:10:15.632
in America is designed, that you

00:10:15.965 --> 00:10:17.167
have to find compromise.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.868
The American people made a

00:10:19.002 --> 00:10:21.271
decision to have the Republicans

00:10:21.404 --> 00:10:22.338
in power in the house.

00:10:22.472 --> 00:10:24.073
The Democrats have a small

00:10:24.207 --> 00:10:25.542
majority in the senate, and the

00:10:25.975 --> 00:10:26.943
Democrats have a president.

00:10:27.076 --> 00:10:29.245
But we're all Americans, and we

00:10:29.379 --> 00:10:30.513
all have to work together.

00:10:30.647 --> 00:10:33.449
But the one thing I do know, our

00:10:33.583 --> 00:10:34.984
debt is too high.

00:10:35.118 --> 00:10:37.587
We have waste in our government.

00:10:37.987 --> 00:10:40.890
And we need to sit down

00:10:41.024 --> 00:10:42.392
together, in a responsible way,

